From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: video decoders for HEVC Main and Main10, and no wait
 for the GPU each picture

HEVC Main (NV12) and Main 10 (P010) decoders on Vulkan Video
(VK_KHR_video_decode_h265), beside H.264: DXVA_PicParams_HEVC and its
scaling lists are turned into the standard's VPS, SPS and PPS, the
picture's reference sets (DXVA's RefPicList indices) into DPB slots.
Profiles are listed per codec (D3D11VideoDecodeSupport::Profiles), each
with its DXGI and Vulkan format; HEVC's short slices are
ConfigBitstreamRaw 1.

The decoder no longer waits on the CPU for each picture's decode before
the next: four frames in flight, each with its own bitstream buffer,
command buffer and session parameters, and only the one reused four
pictures later is waited for. The GPU still orders decode and DXVK's copy
(timeline semaphores, as before).

Offered only where proven, as H.264 (d3d11.videoDecode). Bit-exact
against FFmpeg's software decoder on NVIDIA's driver.
